# Trivy allowlist — Phase 21αβ.H8 / 24.3
#
# One CVE per line; # for comments. Mirrors the pip-audit-ignore.txt
# shape so the conventions are symmetric.
#
# Workflow: a CVE lands here ONLY when:
#   1. The CVE applies to a transitive OS package we can't directly
#      pin (e.g. a libpython CVE on the Debian base image)
#   2. There's no upstream fix yet
#   3. The justification is a one-line comment naming the package +
#      reason (e.g. "# CVE-XXXX-NNNN: libssl3, no fix in bookworm")
#
# All entries should be reviewed quarterly. A CVE that gets fixed
# upstream should be removed promptly so we catch the next batch.

# (no entries — empty baseline as of 2026-06-13)
